  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 RNA encoder dominates (0.706-0.725 vs 0.52-0.54 for scgpt), and among scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l configs, transformer aggregation with weighted fusion (config_007, 0.725) is the current best. The only untested variation on this top-performing axis is the fusion strategy. This experiment tests whether concat fusion (config_036) can outperform weighted fusion when paired with transformer aggregation and the best image encoder. It is a minimal, targeted exploitation of the strongest evidence: only one parameter changes from the best result, so any accuracy difference is cleanly attributable to fusion. Expected cost is comparable to config_007 (~3.5-4 GPU hours) since architecture (transformer aggregation, multiprofile, multimodal) is identical. With 4 experiments remaining, confirming or improving the fusion choice on the top configuration is the highest-value next step before exploring image-encoder swaps."
